# No Native Select Controls in Modals

<rule>
name: no_modal_native_select_controls
description: Modal and confirmation dialogs must not use native radio buttons, checkbox lists, or bare select elements for choosing one option from many. Use the existing custom-dropdown pattern instead.

## Why

- `.modal-content input { width: 100% }` and global `appearance: none` rules break native radios/checkboxes into full-width bars.
- StaticForge already has a shared dropdown system documented in `dropdown-setup.mdc`.

## Forbidden in modals / confirmation dialogs

- `<input type="radio">` lists for schedule or enum pickers
- `<input type="checkbox">` lists when only one value should be chosen
- Raw `<select>` for styled settings UI (unless explicitly approved legacy code)

## Required pattern

Use the existing dropdown markup and JS:

```html
<div class="custom-dropdown dropup">
    <button type="button" class="custom-dropdown-btn hover-show colored">
        <span id="mySettingSelected">Current label</span>
    </button>
    <div id="mySettingMenu" class="custom-dropdown-menu hidden"></div>
</div>
<input type="hidden" id="mySettingHidden" value="">
```

Wire with `setupDropdown` + `renderGroupedDropdown` or `renderSimpleDropdown` from `public/scripts/comp/dropdown.js`. Read the saved value from the hidden input in `resolveValue` or the save handler.

## After dialog HTML is injected

Call wiring in `setTimeout(..., 0)` immediately after `showConfirmationDialog` / `showInputDialog` starts (same pattern as `wireRestartBroomToggleInDialog` in logViewerApplet.js).

## Reference

- `public/scripts/comp/dropdown.js`
- `.cursor/rules/dropdown-setup.mdc`
- Fixed example: `wireQuipsAutoUpdateScheduleDropdown` in `public/scripts/comp/generationQuipsTray.js`
</rule>
